{
  "_about": [
    "Chapter 3, rescue at headquarters. This file is the palette block \"ch3\" (levels pick it with \"palette\": \"ch3\").",
    "Look: close to pitch black inside an office tower with the power out, and on its roof. The tower is three levels, one file each: web/levels/ch3.json (ground floor), ch3_2f.json (first floor up) and ch3_roof.json. It starts from the chosen mood (heavy) and changes what that look needs; every difference is explained in the PR description.",
    "Almost nothing shows outside the flashlight beam. The guide colour is the orange of the fuel barrels; red emergency lamps pulse on the walls.",
    "greybox.ch3Fire / ch3Lamp are the warm emitters built by web/js/props/Ch3Props.js: color and intensity of the glowing surface (above 1 feeds the bloom), light = the point light that reaches a few metres around it, flicker = how much the fire wavers. ch3Led is the small cold glow of the server racks.",
    "Dynamic lights: flashlight + bin fire + work lamp + one emergency beacon (alarm.light.count 1) = 4, the limit. That is why the moon and the barrel glow light are switched off here.",
    "greybox.surfaces: the office floors use textures painted by art/textures/ch3/generate.py (carpet tiles, painted wall, suspended ceiling). \"rough\" names the roughness map that web/js/props/Ch3Props.js adds on top; the wall tile is as tall as a wall (3.2 m) so its skirting board sits on the floor. The roof keeps concrete: see ch3_roof.json."
  ],
